# What ships to a consumer, and what stays in the repository.
#
# A Composer dist is built from the tag's tracked tree, so without these lines every
# install of every package carries the test suite and the architecture fixtures with it:
# mahout-devtools alone shipped 350 files, 207 of them fixtures that deliberately contain
# banned patterns (raw superglobals outside the request boundary, unbounded statements,
# a second host touching superglobals). Those files declare classes in the family's own
# namespaces, so a consumer's autoloader census, its search for a symbol, and a static
# analysis run that globs vendor/ all meet code that exists only to prove a gate fires.
# The rule that a fixture demonstrates is not the rule the fixture is evidence for; the
# evidence belongs in the repository, not in the deployed vendor tree.
#
# What stays shipped is exactly what consumers reference, verified rather than assumed:
#   src/, rules/, bin/, stubs/, resources/, templates/  - code, and the rules the arch gate loads
#   phpstan.neon, phpstan-base.neon, phpstan-arch.neon   - the host's phpstan.neon includes them
#   rector.php, psalm.xml, .php-cs-fixer.dist.php        - shared config, referenced not copied (19 6)
#   docs/, languages/, and the artifact set              - README/CHANGELOG/LICENSE/AGENTS and POT files
# phpstan-arch.neon's parameters.paths is src and rules, and the fixer resolves its paths
# from the consumer's getcwd() with a per-repository .php-cs-fixer.paths.php override, so
# nothing here is consulted at the consumer's expense.

/.github/		export-ignore
/.gitignore		export-ignore
/composer.lock		export-ignore
/tests/			export-ignore
/fixtures/		export-ignore
/phpunit.xml.dist	export-ignore
/phpstan-arch-fixtures.neon	export-ignore
